// The battle of the showcase's effects take (assets/captures/showcase.ron, take `effects`; plan
// docs/plans/2026-11-09-effect-visualization.md, WP14 and Amendment 31).
//
// Player 0 fields a siege line that holds where it spawns, in a row beside its hall: every unit with
// a mode switch anchors or burrows at once (EnterModes; a unit with earlier orders would switch
// after them). Player 0 is given no attack-move, so its burrowing units stay in the line (an
// attack-move takes every unit with an A command, unarmed ones included; plan
// docs/plans/2026-11-24-attack-orders.md D-6). Player 0's other units have no orders and fight
// where they stand. Player 1's
// raiders attack-move into the line, towards player 0's base. The take is its own battle, so
// the `battle` take's scenario, outcome and winner are unchanged.
(
    format_version: 1,
    map: "maps/showcase_canyon.scmap.ron",
    seed: 1592639215,
    players: [
        (player_slot: 0, loadout_slug: "showcase_siege_line"),
        (player_slot: 1, loadout_slug: "showcase_raiders"),
    ],
    initial_orders: [
        EnterModes(player_slot: 0),
        AttackMoveToCell(player_slot: 1, cell: (11, 11)),
    ],
